course: dictionary
lesson: 6793
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «In 1862 Charles Darwin looked at an orchid whose nectar sat at the bottom of a tube about thirty centimetres long.» Nectar and tube are clues that orchid is a flower here.
explain: Now look for different clues. «Her scarf was a pale orchid colour» uses orchid as a colour, not a plant. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
fact: An orchid is a beautiful flower with petals of unusual shapes.
fact: There are many thousands of kinds of orchid; «there are about 28000 kinds of orchid».
fact: Orchid is also a pale purple colour, so a dress or a wall can be orchid.
fact: «Epiphytes such as orchids, ferns and bromeliads live on branches high up», catching rain and fallen bits instead of rooting in soil.
fact: «The orchid mantis looks like a flower», and some insects are even more attracted to it than to real flowers.
exercise: What is an orchid? | A kind of bird that lives in deserts | A tall tree that grows by the sea | *A beautiful flower with petals of unusual shapes | A large, slow fish
exercise: «Epiphytes such as orchids, ferns and bromeliads live on branches high up, catching rain.» Where do epiphytes live? | *On branches high up | Deep inside rocks | Under the sea | In the soil
exercise: Which colour is orchid? | *A pale purple | A bright yellow, like a lemon | A bright red, like a fire engine | A deep black
test: «Charles Darwin said a moth with a tongue that long must exist.» The orchid's nectar sat at the bottom of what? | *A tube about thirty centimetres long | A pond | A cup of tea | A tree trunk
test: «Some animals copy a thing: an orchid mantis looks like a pink flower.» What is the mantis copying? | A dead leaf | A stick | A stone | *A pink flower
exam: Which sentence uses orchid as a colour? | Bees visited the orchid in the garden | Charles Darwin studied an orchid in 1862 | *Her scarf was a lovely orchid colour | The orchid grew on a tall tree in the forest
